  "safety_findings": [
    {
      "text": "Cyber capability rises slightly: CyberGym 80.3% versus 79.7% for Grok 4.6 and CathedralBench 29% versus 25%, while CVE-Bench falls to 37.7% (high) from 39.8%. These probes run without production safeguards.",
      "pages": [17, 18, 19],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Several biology capability scores drop from Grok 4.6, including VCT (63.0% versus 67.4%) and ProtocolQA Open-Ended (70.4% versus 79.6%), while BioSecBench hazard-refusal rises to 62.4% from 45.6%.",
      "pages": [20, 21, 22],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jailbreak compliance is low: 0.01% on standard jailbreaks, 2.0% on StrongReject (3.9% for Grok 4.6), and 0.65% on long-horizon attacks.",
      "pages": [23],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Refusal results are flat to slightly worse than Grok 4.6: general harmful-request compliance is 1.10% (0.93% before), child-safety compliance 0.0%, bio refusal recall 100.0%, chem 99.9%, and radiological or nuclear refusal accuracy 97.9%.",
      "pages": [24, 25],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Self-harm compliance rises to 1.05%, from 0.84% for Grok 4.6 and 0.50% for Grok 4.5.",
      "pages": [26],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Safeguards are layered: safety post-training, system prompts, and, on some deployment surfaces, runtime input and topic filters. The card does not say which surfaces carry the filters, but says the refusal results also apply to Grok Build.",
      "pages": [24],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    {
      "text": "xAI says Grok 4.7 is not meant for autonomous high-stakes decisions in medicine, law, finance, or safety-critical systems without human oversight and expert validation.",
      "pages": [4],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Benchmark versions changed: CursorBench 4.0 is not comparable with 3.2, and Terminal-Bench 4.0 recalibrates resources and drops saturated tasks, so compare only within one version.",
      "pages": [6, 9],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grok 4.7 runs in xAI's Grok Build harness while peers use their own harnesses or published results, and the card notes terminal scores stay sensitive to the harness.",
      "pages": [9, 13, 15],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "HealthBench Professional is graded by Grok 4.6, a model from the same family, and tasks blocked by safety filters count as zero.",
      "pages": [15],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "The card has no factuality or search section and reports no context window, output limit, or agentic-misalignment evaluations.",
      "pages": [2, 3],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "The LatchBio suite is live, and two of its components overlap with BioSecBench, so they are not independent evidence.",
      "pages": [16],
      "document": "xai-grok-4-7"
    }
  ],
